  "area_source": "Agreste SAA departmental area series, mean of campaigns 2022-2024.",
  "arable_ha_definition": "Agreste COP subtotals summed: all cereals (LIB_SAA 27) + all oilseeds (36) + all grain legumes (46). Uses the published subtotals, not a re-addition of the crops this project models, so the denominator cannot drift with the crop mapping. Still not total UAA: silage maize, root crops, potatoes and fodder sit outside this sheet.",
  "pulse_ha_definition": "Agreste LIB_SAA row 46, total proteagineux et legumes secs cultives pour leur graine: pea, fava bean, lentil, chickpea, dry bean, lupin and residual categories. Excludes dehydrated alfalfa and temporary grassland, which were more than half the 2020 baseline of the French protein-crop target and are forage, not food. Soybean is reported separately in soybean_ha because Agreste classes it as an oilseed.",
  "centroid_source": "Cadastral-area-weighted mean of IGN ADMINEXPRESS commune centroids.",
  "removed_fields_note": "No per-department irrigation share is emitted. An earlier version wrote 42 hand-written percentages here with no source; nothing consumed them, and an undefendable number in reference data is worse than none. Irrigation enters the engine where it is actually evidenced, in refdata/irrigation.json, which decomposes Agreste's blended irrigated and rain-fed yields using national irrigated-area shares per crop.",
  "national_target": {
   "current_pulse_share_pct": 4.0,
   "target_pulse_share_pct": 8.0,
   "target_year": 2030
  }
